WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.120
Hey guys,
In this video, we're going to take a look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:09.540
at what the Bible says about how men should dress.
And how they should take care of their appearance.&nbsp;

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.700
Now, I know some of you might be thinking,&nbsp;
Daniel, the Bible doesn't say anything about this.&nbsp;

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.380
Well, you're wrong.
The Bible has a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:25.920
to say about how we present ourselves to the&nbsp;
world which will become clear in this video.&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:33.720
And this will shock many of you, because preachers&nbsp;
never talk about it or at least I haven't heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.180
a preacher talk about this in my whole life.
Now, you need to know that you can be a stumbling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:45.480
block to an unbeliever, pushing them away from&nbsp;
the Gospel, just because of your appearance.&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.320
Yeah, let me explain.
There are too many Christian men that look sloppy.&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.200
Unprofessional.
Lazy.&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.320
And who don't care about their appearance at all.
You know, it is great that God is not like man.&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.380
Not like human beings.
Because He doesn't judge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.560
based on our outside appearance.
What we look like.&nbsp;

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.260
You know, we always say this:&nbsp;
Don't judge a book by its cover.&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.680
But we do this.
We humans, because we are not perfect.&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.740
We are not God.
God - now He looks at your heart.&nbsp;

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.720
Your intentions.
Your character.&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.040
And that's how He judges you.
But we missed the part where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.660
the Bible also says that men judge&nbsp;
according to the outside appearance.&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.600
Because they can't see right through you.
They're not God.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.460
[1 Samuel 16:7]

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.060
Now most of the time, when people&nbsp;
read this, they just focus on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.260
part where it says that God judges the heart.
But they totally just leave out the part that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.960
says that man focuses on the outside appearance.
And this is important for us to understand.&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.500
I'm going to explain to you why I'm&nbsp;
mentioning this a little bit later on.&nbsp;

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.880
But first I need to make this very clear.
Because I don't want you to misunderstand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.820
the point I'm trying to make.
Vanity is a sin.&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.520
And it is a lot more important to focus&nbsp;
on the inside than on the outside.&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.040
Spiritual growth.
That's a lot more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.900
important than just focusing on your outside&nbsp;
appearance, which will just return to dust anyway.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.460
[Genesis 3:19]

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.260
So let me ask you, if you are God's&nbsp;
ambassador, living in His temple,&nbsp;

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.580
your body.
And people look at you when you represent God,&nbsp;

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.400
what do they see?
Their first impressions?&nbsp;

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.860
Someone who looks modest?
Who looks respectful?&nbsp;

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.720
Or someone who dresses in a way that&nbsp;
is flashy and attention-seeking.&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.780
Someone who professes to be a Christian&nbsp;
but is so self-absorbed that they don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.200
realize they're worshiping&nbsp;
themselves instead of God.&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:04.380
So I want to be very clear on this.
Dressing to impress for the wrong reasons.&nbsp;

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.280
Being vain.
Aiming to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:15.180
guy who always wants the best and most costly&nbsp;
expensive brands, because of vanity, is wrong.&nbsp;

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.420
Or if you do it because you think&nbsp;
it improves your self-worth.&nbsp;

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:23.760
It is wrong, because your&nbsp;
self-worth is only found in God.&nbsp;

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:31.320
Vanity makes you self-absorbed,&nbsp;
arrogant, puffed-up, and selfish.&nbsp;

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:37.680
And can lead to envy, strife&nbsp;
and, well, an empty and sad life.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.540
[Proverbs 16:18]

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.820
Now, what I'm talking about in this&nbsp;
video is all the way to the other side.&nbsp;

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.620
The other extreme.
Men.&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.040
Christian men.
Who think that they shouldn't take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.740
care of their appearance at all.
So they don't groom.&nbsp;

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.200
They don't look modest.
They don't look respectful.&nbsp;

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.960
For example, if you want to&nbsp;
share the Gospel to someone.&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.540
You're walking towards them.
They see you.&nbsp;

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.080
They already start to make judgments&nbsp;
on you based on your appearance.&nbsp;

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.260
Man, this guy who looks sloppy.
It doesn't look respectful at all.&nbsp;

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.020
He doesn't look modest.
I don't want anything to do with him.&nbsp;

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:27.120
So they already decide there and then&nbsp;
that they don't want to listen to you.&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.020
So how are you going to share the Gospel to&nbsp;
them if they are already negative towards you?&nbsp;

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:35.220
Nowhere in scripture does it say that you&nbsp;
should not take care of your appearance.&nbsp;

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.380
It does say that your character is&nbsp;
more important and we all know that.&nbsp;

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.840
But it also says a great deal about how&nbsp;
you present yourself to other people.&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.080
I mean, you are God's ambassador.&nbsp;

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.100
Paul says...
[1 Corinthians 9:20-21]

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.540
Now listen to this.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.800
[1 Corinthians 9:22]

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.640
You can't dress sloppy and go to talk to&nbsp;
someone who is very worldly and thinks about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:52.380
the importance of appearance all the time.
Who's so self-absorbed that just wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:55.740
wear designer brands all the time.
They probably wouldn't even want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.620
to start listening to you.
And you can't dress in a nice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:03.720
suit to talk to a homeless person.
You gotta think, yes, it is sad.&nbsp;

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:08.880
But this is the world that we live&nbsp;
in, all humans, not one is perfect.&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.500
And so people make assumptions based&nbsp;
on the appearance of other people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:19.500
People have sinful natures and those&nbsp;
sinful natures will judge you wrongly.&nbsp;

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:24.480
So dress according to the&nbsp;
occasion in order to save souls.&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.980
Don't always just dress like&nbsp;
a church person but dress more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:34.860
in line with those who you are trying to save.
If you don't connect with people on their level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:38.640
then you'll be an obstacle&nbsp;
for them to hear the Gospel.&nbsp;

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.660
And you have to do it.
As you do everything now.&nbsp;

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.660
Because we're under the law of the&nbsp;
Spirit, which means everything you do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:50.580
now should be through the Spirit, meaning&nbsp;
everything you do should be done for God.&nbsp;

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.260
Even normal things, like eating and drinking.
For example ...

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.280
[1 Corinthians 10:31]

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.020
Now some of you might say, ah come on&nbsp;
Daniel, something as basic as food and drink?&nbsp;

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.580
How do we do that for God?
First of all, it's not me who says it.&nbsp;

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.660
It's God's word that says this.
And when we look at something as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:25.560
basic as food and drink, you need to&nbsp;
ask yourself, how much food do I eat?&nbsp;

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:29.280
Am I addicted to food?
A glutton?&nbsp;

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:34.440
Or am I so worried about my appearance&nbsp;
that I don't eat enough to live healthy?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:40.140
And do I pray before I eat and thank&nbsp;
God for the food that he's given me?&nbsp;

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.860
So yes, even in the food and drink&nbsp;
that we consume we have to honor God.&nbsp;

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.300
And that goes for everything you do.
Everything must be done through the Spirit.&nbsp;

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.700
And that includes taking care of your appearance.
Some of you might still be asking, Daniel what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.280
does this have to do with my appearance?
What is my faith?&nbsp;

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.700
What does that have to do with my appearance?&nbsp;

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.900
Everything!
Your appearance is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:09.480
reflection of your inner character.
A new creation that is different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:13.800
from the person you used to be.
Now, you dress in a way that is modest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.440
respectful, and you are showing the&nbsp;
world that you are a man of faith.&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.760
So we should take care of our appearance.
We should groom ourselves properly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.020
and keep ourselves clean.
Hygienic, healthy.&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:34.380
You should also dress more respectable so that&nbsp;
other people will feel more inclined to go and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:38.640
talk to you, especially if you want to share&nbsp;
the Gospel to them. They want to feel, man, I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:45.120
feel that I could just go and talk to this person.
This person feels warm, open, modest, respectable.&nbsp;

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.000
There's something about this person.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.340
[1 Timothy 2:9-10]

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:12.660
Did you see that?
Your appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:17.940
that goes together with your good works.
That is what you are showing to the world.&nbsp;

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:23.700
Now, I know Paul wrote this to women, right?
But does it not apply to men as well?&nbsp;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.960
Today men can also dress in a&nbsp;
way that does not honor God.&nbsp;

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:33.840
And the Greek word here&nbsp;
used for modesty is kosmios.&nbsp;

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.840
And the same word is used when you talk to men.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.580
[1 Timothy 3:2]

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:57.180
So your appearance is important.
Dressing modestly is for men and women.&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.140
The Bible even talks about bodily training.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:02.520
[1Timothy 4:8]

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:17.700
Yes or no, training in godliness, growing&nbsp;
spiritually, you know really connecting to God.&nbsp;

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.100
God sees your heart.
That is a lot more important than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:26.340
what's going on your outside appearance.
But you cannot live selfishly.&nbsp;

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:29.460
Oh, it's just me and my relationship with God.
What about other people?&nbsp;

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:33.180
You are called to share the Gospel.
So to do that, you cannot be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:36.600
a stumbling block for other people.
You need to connect with them at their level.&nbsp;

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:44.220
And even though spiritual growth is important -&nbsp;
more important than bodily training - it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:49.200
say here that bodily training is not important.
It says that it is of some value.&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.540
Now, some of you might be thinking, wow, did&nbsp;
they train their bodies in the time of the Bible?&nbsp;

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:55.080
Yes.&nbsp;

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.620
Don't think you're something special&nbsp;
because you live 2000 years later.&nbsp;

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.920
There's nothing new under the sun.
They also had athletes.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.840
[1 Corinthians 9:25]

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:16.800
Now, how can you be the light of the world?
A sweet smelling aroma, live peaceably with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:22.260
all people, if people don't even want to talk&nbsp;
to you because you don't use deodorant - you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.080
smell - and you don't groom?
You look like someone who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:30.960
lazy, not respectable at all.
No, you need to be the light of the world.&nbsp;

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:35.400
They need to be able to think, man this&nbsp;
person, there's something about this person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:40.620
I want ... to get to know this person.
Who are they, what are they thinking.&nbsp;

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:44.460
They look like someone who's modest, respectable.
Jesus says...

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.000
[Matthew 5:14]

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.320
Now of course, like I said, shining your&nbsp;
light goes hand in hand with your actions.&nbsp;

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.220
So your appearance and your actions, the&nbsp;
example that you set to non-believers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:06.240
all those things work together.
And of course, you cannot do it if you don't share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.660
the gospel through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Because it is not us who are changing lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.420
it is Jesus Christ.
And only He can do that through people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:15.840
who are preaching through the Holy Spirit.
So don't do it through the flesh.&nbsp;

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:20.040
And next time, when you prepare yourself&nbsp;
in the morning, you're getting ready,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:23.280
you're getting groomed, remember&nbsp;
to dress according to the occasion.&nbsp;

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:30.900
Work on your appearance in such a way that&nbsp;
is modest, respectful, and also appropriate.&nbsp;

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:36.540
Now, if you want more videos - more advice&nbsp;
for men - then please watch these videos here.&nbsp;

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:41.520
And I'll see you there.
And always remember - life is short,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:45.420
so don't waste yours.
Bye guys.

